        <p>Day after day without giving heed to their suffering, should beari n mind that the human body, like a machine of steel or wood, will, if overdriven, break down completely some day. Over- straining can't go on indefinitely. If your household duties feel to tire you unduly, if tasks which used to be light now seem to fag you out, look to it. Be sure somethmg is wrong with those great foundations of health the liver and the digestive organs. A course of Bile Beans, if taken in time, will prevent any serious illness, but if you dally, who can answer for the result? Mrs. Harkness, of Kirk Street, Calton, Glasgow, says: "After my boy was born I did not recover my strength. My digestion failed, and I had frequent attacks of biliousness. My breathing grew heavy and laboured, my sleep left me, and I became so weak as to be absolutely unfit for any work. Doctors' medicine proved of no avail, and I was reduced to such a sorry plight that for several years I did not once go out of the house! It was more to please my daughter than in any hope of a cure, that I tried Bile Beans, but I had only taken a short course when I felt an improvement. I persevered, and am glad to say that I am now enjoying good health." For general weakness, rheumatism, debility, anaamia, indigestion constipa- tion, piles, liver complaint; and all female ailments, Bile Beans are un- equalled. Of all Cfiemists,. at 1/1i or 2,9 per box. If you are ailing, don't delay, but</p>
