        <p>LONGFORD HOTEL CLUB.</p>
        <p>A supper was given at the above hotel the ether Miffl- in to celehra'e the close of the green for the season, upwards of 40 members sitting down to an excellent repast grovided by the h Ist and hostess, Mr and Mrs Horloelr. Afterwares a sr:finking concert was held when Mr G Maywell was voted ti Ulu cliair,and was supported by Mr William Pemberton and Mr Croohsbank. Mr J Pemberton presiding at the piano. Various songs and toasts were given awl a very enjoyable evening, was spent, the following gentlemen contributing to the programme :—Messrs Atherton. Maxwell, William Pem- berton, Pat Huehan, Daglanb, G Higbam, Kearns, Fred Dean and William Dean. The prneeedings env) brought to a close by tI2O singing of the National Anthem.</p>
        <p>Presentation to Mr. Levi Richardson.</p>
        <p>At the close of the lessons on Sunday afternoon, at the Ellesmere-street Wesleysn Methodist Sunday School, Mr Levi Richardson was the recipient of a small wedding present as a token of the eszeem in which he is held at the above schools. The presen- tation, which consisted of a pair of bronze figures and an inkstand, was made on behalf uf the school by Mr John Ellison, who alluded to the early asso- ciations of Mr Richardson with the school when it was in its infancy. Mr Richardson,in ackcowledging this token of respect, said he always had thought, and ever should think kindly about Ellesmere.street School. He held in his hand a silver pencil case which was given him at that school some ten years ago, amd'he prized it as much as the more costly presents he haalreceived because of the loving spirit in which it was given, and equally PO would he look on the figures of the spirited horses which he had pleasure in accepting on behalf of Mrs Richardson and himself that day. Mr Sherburn (superintendent) said he had listened with pleasure to the bit of early history of the school and its workers in the days gone by. On ehalf of the school he wished Mr and Mrs Richardson long life and much happiness.- Medals for a Local Officer.</p>
        <p>The Commander-in-Chiet has awarded the Army medal for long service and good conduct to Sergeant-Major W. Delmage of the South Lanco• shire liegiment.</p>
