        <p>WARRINGTON WATER. VIRW OF THE, POSSIBILITY THAT ALARM. MAY HAVR BEEN CREATED among tke inhabitants of Warrinzton by recent reports with reference to the water supply, it is well that I should make it publicly known that the condition of the water is not only a continual care of the I Health Department. but has been under special observation of late. The result of recent examination by the Bacterio logist who acts for the Corporation is to show that the pre sent condition of the water as excellent. This is borne out by the fact that there is no wide spread epithmic of typhoid fever, one of the most likely diseases to be water borne ; in fact, there is much less of this disease than is usual at this time of the year, I would aid that no vigilance will be ' wanting on the part of this Department in trying to detect any danger to the town from its water supply. 3.11. GORNALL,, Medical Officer of Health,</p>
