        <p>At Hessenford, near Liskeard, on Wednesday morning two lads, John Moon, aged ten, and Willie Symms smged four, were playing with a double-barrelled gun in a barn,when the weapon was accidently dischargetkilling Symons instantly. Moon had no auspicien that the gun was loaded. Symons's father, distra3ted by grief, threatened to kill himself, his wife and the other child, and hod to be restrained by the police.</p>
