      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-10-17_WidnesExaminer_art0094" n="art0094">
        <head>"THE FOOD THAT IS ALL FOOD."</head>
        <p>"THE FOOD THAT IS ALL FOOD."</p>
        <p>Bodily troubles speedily disappear when "FORCE" is eaten. The whole-wheat and 'barley-malt, of which the food is composed, "tone up" the system. In thig• way the bodily organs are enabled to do their work properly; and once this condition of affairs has been set up, any derangement from which the system may be -iiffering must speedily vanish.—" FORCE" requires no cooking. per large package. Ask the grocer.</p>
